## Schema
```bash
cat > online_disable_misc_fixed.ldif <<-EOF
dn: cn={4}misc,cn=schema,cn=config
changetype: modify
replace: olcObjectClasses
# 辅助类：保留原有属性，添加合理但严苛的必填属性（MUST cn，实际没有，等效禁用）
olcObjectClasses: {0}( 2.16.840.1.113730.3.2.147 NAME 'inetLocalMailRecipient'
DESC 'Internet local mail recipient' SUP top AUXILIARY MUST cn MAY (
mailLocalAddress $ mailHost $ mailRoutingAddress ) )
# 结构类：改为ABSTRACT抽象类，无法直接创建条目
olcObjectClasses: {1}( 1.3.6.1.4.1.42.2.27.1.2.5 NAME 'nisMailAlias' DESC 'NIS
mail alias' SUP top ABSTRACT MUST cn MAY rfc822MailMember )
EOF

ldapmodify -Y EXTERNAL -H ldapi:/// -f online_disable_misc_fixed.ldif
```

LDAP Schema defines what data can be stored in the directory. It specifies valid attributes, value formats, matching rules, and object classes. An object class determines what an entry is and which attributes are required or optional. Multiple compatible object classes, such as inetOrgPerson and posixAccount, can be combined in one entry.


## Verification 

LDAP authentication is usually performed through a Bind operation using a DN and password, or through SASL. Passwords may be stored as SSHA hashes, while SSL/TLS protects credentials and LDAP data during transmission. LDAPS uses TLS from the beginning, usually on port 636, while StartTLS upgrades a normal LDAP connection on port 389.


